<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Matrix and image under a shear</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A shear has the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis invariant and shear factor \({@k@}\).</p><p>(a) Write down its matrix.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the image of the point \(({@p[1]@},\,{@p[2]@})\).</p><div>( [[input:ans2]] , [[input:ans3]] ) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Every point slides parallel to the invariant axis, by the shear factor times its distance from that axis, so areas do not change.</p><p>(a) With the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis invariant, (1, 0) and (0, 1) go to the columns of \({@ta@}\): [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]\(x' = {@x+k*y@}\) and \(y' = y\).[[else]]\(x' = x\) and \(y' = {@y+k*x@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) The point's [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]y[[else]]x[[/if]]-coordinate, \({@dist@}\), is its signed distance from the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis, so it slides \({@k@} \times [[if test="is(dist<0)"]]({@dist@})[[else]]{@dist@}[[/if]] = {@k*dist@}\) parallel to the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis: \({@ta@}{@pc@} = {@ta.pc@}\). The image is \(({@tp[1]@},\,{@tp[2]@})\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
near(L,T) := is(abs(L[1]-T[1]) + abs(L[2]-T[2]) < 0.001);
/* Design: matrix and image under a shear, in the chapter's wording (invariant axis, shear factor). Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), Chapter 13, Section 6 and Chapter 14, Section 6. The other position, the stretch confusion and "moved by k only" give images distinct from the answer and each other. */
slist: [["x",4,[-1,4]],["y",-4,[-1,4]],["x",1/2,[1,4]],["y",-1/2,[2,3]],["x",3/2,[1,2]],["y",-3/2,[3,-2]],["x",5/2,[3,-1]],["y",1,[-1,4]],["x",-1,[1,4]],["y",5,[2,4]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
ax: slist[ix][1]; k: slist[ix][2]; p: slist[ix][3];
pc: transpose(matrix(p));
ta: if ax="x" then matrix([1,k],[0,1]) else matrix([1,0],[k,1]);
/* diagnostics: k in the other position; a stretch; the point moved by k, not k times its distance */
dW: if ax="x" then matrix([1,0],[k,1]) else matrix([1,k],[0,1]);
dSt: if ax="x" then matrix([1,0],[0,k]) else matrix([k,0],[0,1]);
tp: list_matrix_entries(ta.pc); pW: list_matrix_entries(dW.pc); pSt: list_matrix_entries(dSt.pc);
pK: if ax="x" then [p[1]+k,p[2]] else [p[1],p[2]+k];
dist: if ax="x" then p[2] else p[1];
tw: ta+matrix([0,0],[0,1]); tpw: tp+[0,1];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, axis {@ax@}, k={@k@}, image={@tp@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Matrices and Transformations: matrix and image under a shear</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.1: Write down the matrix of a shear with a given invariant axis and shear factor, and find the image of a point.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 13, Section 6 and Chapter 14, Section 6 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: the shear given by its invariant axis and shear factor in this book's wording, new factors and points, randomised, with named and follow-through feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
